# Unit Testing Job Rule

## Critical Rules

### Related Rules
This rule must be used in conjunction with:
- [Testing General Principles](.cursor/rules/manual/testing-general-principles.mdc) - For fundamental testing principles and practices
- [Unit Testing Best Practices](.cursor/rules/manual/unit-testing-best-practices.mdc) - For general unit testing best practices

### Jobs
**Guidelines:**
- Test that the job calls the expected repository/model methods.
- Test that the job handles empty or invalid data gracefully.
- Test that the job performs the expected side effects (e.g., deletes, updates).
- Test that the job does not throw exceptions for valid input.

### Example
```php
public function testHandleDeletesFiles()
{
    $mockFile = $this->createPartialMock(StorageFile::class, ['forceDelete', 'newModelQuery']);
    $mockFile->expects($this->once())->method('forceDelete');
    $queryBuilder = resolve(\Illuminate\Database\Query\Builder::class);
    $eloquentBuilder = $this->getMockBuilder(\Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Builder::class)
        ->setConstructorArgs([$queryBuilder])
        ->onlyMethods(['cursor'])
        ->getMock();
    $eloquentBuilder->method('cursor')->willReturn(new LazyCollection([$mockFile]));
    $mockFile->method('newModelQuery')->willReturn($eloquentBuilder);
    $this->partialMock(FileRepositoryInterface::class, function ($mock) use ($mockFile) {
        $mock->allows('getModel')->andReturns($mockFile);
    });
    $job = new CleanUpDeletedStorageFiles();
    $job->handle();
}
```
